body: "## Summary\n\nReview of a new caller of the reusable Daily Release (pm-ado#131, pinned to v2026.11.22, `1d9f9daba721f2cb8bec4aef69ca54402b08350e`) raised an interruption point in `daily-release.ts` that the callers cannot fix:\n\nIf a candidate refresh is cancelled **after the force-push of the release branch and before the release PR body (the receipt) is updated**, the PR points at the new head while its receipt still names the old head. The next run refuses the head mismatch. `retire-unpublished` applies the same head check, so it cannot clear the state either. The release stays blocked after the original cause is gone.\n\nThis is a sibling of #314 (an interrupted `retire-unpublished` cannot be completed by a retry): both are a two-step transition with no record that lets a later run finish or roll back the first step.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The refresh records its intended head transition (old head, new head, run id) before the force-push, in a place the next run reads, so a later run can finish the receipt update for exactly that transition or roll the branch back.\n- An unrelated head change is still refused, and auto-merge is never enabled while the live head and the verified receipt differ.\n- A test interrupts the refresh between the push and the body update and proves that the next scheduled run completes the transition, and that `retire-unpublished` can retire the candidate.\n- All callers get the fix through the normal pin bump; no caller change is needed.\n\n## Scope\n\nEvery package that calls the reusable flow (28 repositories at the moment) inherits this.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-24T21:58:01Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-ops#250 - Free release runners while protected PR checks run [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-25T00:19:51Z)\n>\n> A second interruption point of the same class, from the next review of pm-ado#131: the prepare step pushes `release/VERSION` before `gh pr create`. If the PR creation fails, the branch exists without a PR. A retry that selects the same branch stops at the `retired-branch` check, because there is no PR carrying a retirement receipt, and `retire-unpublished` cannot clear it because it discovers receipts only on PRs. The recorded transition asked for above should cover it: a branch this intent pushed (same version, same head, no PR yet) must be resumable to PR creation, while a foreign branch of that name is still refused. Add a test that fails PR creation after the push and proves the next run opens the PR."
